<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOUTH AFRICA REPORTS 150 WHITE-COLLAR CRIMES A DAY.</title>
<headline>SOUTH AFRICA REPORTS 150 WHITE-COLLAR CRIMES A DAY.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa reported 54,846 cases of white-collar crime last year, Safety and Security Minister Sydney Mufamadi said on Wednesday in reply to a question in parliament.</p>
<p>Most of them -- 22,894 -- were reported in Gauteng, he said, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +2721 403-2502</p>
</text>
